  "user_request_original": "Execute a deterministic Transfer Matrix Method optimization for a planar stack with the following fixed topology: Incident Medium (Air, n=1.0) | Layer 1 (SiO2, n=1.46, lossless) | Layer 2 (TiO2, n=2.40, lossless) | Substrate (Glass, n=1.52, lossless). The stack must contain exactly these two finite layers. Optimize the thickness of Layer 1 and Layer 2, both constrained between 40 nm and 160 nm. The objective is to minimize the arithmetic mean power reflectance for s-polarized light at normal incidence (0 degrees), sampled from 450 nm to 700 nm in 5 nm steps. Use a deterministic grid search or bounded global optimizer with seed 17, allowing up to 64 solver evaluations. Report the optimal thickness pair, the full reflectance spectrum, and the calculated mean reflectance. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization s. wavelength intervals 450-700 nm. soft objectives: minimized arithmetic mean power reflectance in the 450-700 nm band; mean reflectance below 0.03 as a soft scoring preference. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the 450-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: layer thickness bounds: 40 nm to 160 nm; exactly one layer of SiO2 and one layer of TiO2.",
